+// shape-census.mjs — THE ESTATE'S ONE shape-census library (T9-W7; LAWS P6 §I, P7 §C/§F/§I;
+// registry-v7 §2.4 PRODUCT HOME). Every source gate reads the SHAPE through this file, never the
+// spelling, and never through a second reader: a lane that needs a shape this file does not read
+// extends THIS file with the plant that reds it (`--self-test` below), never its own copy.
+// NOT-A-LANE: an importable library plus its browserless self-test; its callers are the source gates that import it (lint:bands, lint:theme-tokens, lint:ink, test:font-coverage on the §13+§7+§3 union) and the pass-8 lanes, cited at docs/tranches/2026-08-tranche-9/evidence/w7/loop/pass7/registry-v7.md §2.4 and pass8/instruments/README.md.
+//
+// LINEAGE. Seeded from MOT-LADDER's product copy on the §13+§7+§3 union (itself the chair's pass-7
+// `instruments/shape-census.mjs`, sha1 3ba7738ee8d4, prettier-formatted, with LADDER's at-rule own
+// declarations), which the union kept as the superset of three vendored copies. Pass 8's batch 0
+// folded every PROPOSED extension registry-v7 §2.4 names into it. Each extension is a CLAUSE with an
+// id: `--self-test` carries the plant that reds it, and `--sabotage-battery` switches each clause off
+// in turn and demands the self-test red (LAWS P7 §F (ii)). The clause ids, by family:
+//   FACE     sfc-toplevel · at-own · wildcard · tw-split · tpl-file · script-css
+//   GRAPHITE tok-sites · tw-arbitrary · at-property-site · r1-dark-arm
+//   TIN      strip-regex · rel-color
+//   LIVE     masked
+//   VERB     is-where-arms · stem-all · setprop-computed · const-carried
+//   SIX      url-dyn · decode · tag-unresolved · h-spread · barrel · pin-binds
+//   WALK     csstext · style-computed-key · import-chain
+//   LADDER   collect-walk · longhand · semicolon-less · clock-arith
+//   ERASE    pcss · register-split
+//   TAPE     element-keyed · tw-utility · closed-context · class-writes · class-ternary · self-close · ws-combinator · param-carried (pass 8, PROPOSED)
+//   LEDGER   media-eval · em-lh · r4-bound
+//   TAB-PEN  html-comment · one-link · token-conflict
+//
+// What it reads (every site a declaration can reach a subject from):
+//   · every TOP-LEVEL <style> block of every SFC (a `<style>` inside a <script> string is never a
+//     stylesheet), every stylesheet in a Vite CSS language (.css .pcss .postcss) under src/ and
+//     public/**, index.html's <style>, and every file an `@import` chain reaches wherever it sits;
+//     comments stripped by a STRING-AWARE (and, for JS, REGEX-LITERAL-AWARE) stripper per language
+//   · nested rules at any depth with their at-rule context, an at-rule's OWN declarations (`@theme`
+//     as :root, `@utility x` as `.x`, `@font-face`/`@property` descriptors), every declaration in
+//     SOURCE ORDER with `!important` read, the last one semicolon-less; a shorthand is a hit on its
